<h2>How I write my notes</h2>
<p>I am <strong>not a doctor, dermatologist or dietitian</strong>, and nothing on this site is medical advice. Here is how I keep my notes careful:</p>
<ul class="chk">
<li>I read systematic reviews and official health sources and link them at the end of every note.</li>
<li>I tell you when the evidence is early, small or only shows an association.</li>
<li>I give real numbers and safe limits, for example for supplements, and I tell you when to see a professional.</li>
<li>I update notes when I learn something new.</li>
</ul>
<p>If you have persistent skin problems, digestive symptoms, or you take medication, please talk to a doctor or dermatologist before changing your routine or diet.</p>

<h2>Honesty and affiliate links</h2>
<p>Some links on this site may be affiliate links, which means I may earn a small commission if you buy through them, at no extra cost to you. I only recommend products I would use myself, and I always say so clearly when a link is an affiliate link.</p>

<h2>Say hi</h2>
<p>Follow along on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/sundayswithanna/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Instagram @sundayswithanna</a>, and join the Sunday letter for one honest recommendation every week.</p>
